---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="AU/NZ Compliance Pack — gate"
  description="Signed attestation and deployment runbooks for gate's AU/NZ PII detection — covering IRD, NHI, TFN, ABN, and Medicare with checksum validation. For FMA, Privacy Act, and APPs compliance."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="tag">AU / NZ Compliance Pack</div>
      <h1>AI data governance for<br />regulated AU/NZ organisations</h1>
      <p>
        gate ships checksum-validated detection for every regulated identifier in
        Australia and New Zealand. The Compliance Pack adds the attestation,
        runbooks, and expert deployment that regulated organisations need to
        demonstrate due diligence to FMA, OAIC, and internal audit.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container" style="padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 4rem;">

    <!-- Identifiers covered -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 3.5rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:1.5rem; letter-spacing:-0.4px;">What's detected</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        Every AU/NZ identifier uses checksum or check-character validation — not just regex.
        This eliminates false positives on numeric strings that happen to match a pattern.
      </p>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>NZ IRD Number</h3>
          <p>Weighted modulus-11 checksum. Covers both 8- and 9-digit formats.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>NZ NHI Number</h3>
          <p>Check-character validation for both legacy (alpha) and new (numeric) NHI formats.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>AU Tax File Number (TFN)</h3>
          <p>Weighted checksum validation. Handles formatting variants (spaces/hyphens).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>AU Business Number (ABN)</h3>
          <p>Weighted modulus-89 checksum. Rejects the majority of false positives at the validation layer.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>AU Medicare Number</h3>
          <p>Luhn-adjacent check digit validation with optional IRN suffix support.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>Standard PII (all regions)</h3>
          <p>Email, phone, full name heuristics, credit card (Luhn), passport patterns, dates of birth.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What the pack adds -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 3.5rem; padding-top: 3rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:1.5rem; letter-spacing:-0.4px;">What the Compliance Pack adds</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        The open-source tool is free and contains all the detection logic.
        The Compliance Pack is for organisations that need to evidence their controls
        to a regulator, auditor, or board.
      </p>

      <div class="steps-grid">
        <div class="step-card">
          <div class="step-num">ASSESS</div>
          <h3>AI data-flow risk assessment</h3>
          <p>
            We map every path where AI agents touch personal information in your environment
            and classify risk by regulator (FMA, OAIC, Privacy Commissioner).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <div class="step-num">DEPLOY</div>
          <h3>Deployment runbook</h3>
          <p>
            Environment-specific installation, configuration review, and forced-column
            mapping for your schema. Tested against your actual query patterns.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <div class="step-num">ATTEST</div>
          <h3>Signed certificate</h3>
          <p>
            GZhu Limited issues a signed attestation that gate is deployed and configured
            correctly for your environment. Suitable for audit evidence and regulator queries.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <div class="step-num">RETAIN</div>
          <h3>Ongoing monitoring</h3>
          <p>
            Quarterly review of patterns against regulatory updates, new AI tool integrations,
            and schema changes. Certificate remains current.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Who it's for -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 3.5rem; padding-top: 3rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:1.5rem; letter-spacing:-0.4px;">Who it's for</h2>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>NZ financial services</h3>
          <p>FMA-regulated firms using AI agents with customer data — wealth management, banking, insurance.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>AU regulated entities</h3>
          <p>APPs-bound organisations under OAIC oversight — financial services, health, telco.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>Government agencies</h3>
          <p>Central and local government adopting AI tooling with access to citizen records.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>Data-heavy tech companies</h3>
          <p>Product teams using AI coding tools (Claude Code, Copilot, Cursor) against production databases.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section style="padding-top: 3rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); text-align: center;">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Start with a conversation</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted); max-width:520px; margin: 0 auto 2rem;">
        The assessment takes one session. If gate isn't the right fit for your environment,
        we'll tell you — the tool is open source and the first conversation is free.
      </p>
      <a href="https://www.gzhu.co.nz/contact.html" class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Talk to GZhu Limited
      </a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
